WEBVTT

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:04.060
Look! Look! Vapor trails!

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:06.230
It's so nice! So nice...

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:07.770
I want to chase after it!

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:09.980
The weather's great; it's refreshing.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:11.650
But it's so hot too!

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:14.700
Then keep your distance!

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:16.620
Get away from me!

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:24.920
You touched my hand when I stretched them out so far...

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:38.720
Just one word is fine.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.560
Just voice your dreams.

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:45.690
It's your first step and first sign to realization.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.770
Ask yourself what is it that you like?

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:51.900
Your answers will...

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:56.910
blow your questions high into the sky.

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:53.320
Even more...

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:55.200
Like fireworks...

00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:03.410
Even though we should all try to be more honest we ourselves, we can't.

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:10.420
Maybe I should try summoning my soul as a child?

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:16.970
What touched my hand when i stretched them out so far...

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:22.100
was a Supernova that suddenly appear to this new night.

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:28.060
For millions of light years, it never stops inside of me.

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:36.280
The longer I gaze, the more power my eyes absorb...

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:41.530
and that's because... because I'm a star too!

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:48.040
With "Old-senpai" in the way,

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:48.040
Hime's love hasn't progressed at all.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:53.050
As Hime worries over her love,

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:53.050
what "shocking statement" does Mihoshi make?

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:55.050
Geez!

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:57.970
What's with her?!

00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:02.560
She's always, <i>always</i> touching Ooyagi-kun! I really envy-

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:05.020
Erm... She's disturbing the class!

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:08.980
I've got no idea what she's thinking - in class or during club activities!

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:12.650
Hime, you sure work hard though.

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:17.150
It's amazing you still haven't given up considering how close those two are.

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:21.070
Well, that's because they're not even going out.

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:22.240
Sure, sure...

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:25.790
You can't carry an unrequited love otherwise, right?

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:27.710
It's true!

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:32.840
But hasn't it become kind of normal for Ooyagi-kun to be seen with his older girlfriend?

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:34.460
They're inseparable.

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:36.590
Ah, that's true.

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:39.510
Girls who like him like that side of him too.

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:40.340
Yup, yup,

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:43.050
they really stimulate my imagination.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.560
Like what are they doing when they're alone together...

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:49.060
I'm sorry, Hime, but we prefer it if they're going out.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:51.350
Mayu! Emily!

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:53.150
Just kidding.

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:55.730
Don't worry. We're on your side.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:56.650
Liars.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:58.150
You're obviously teasing me.

00:02:58.490 --> 00:02:59.990
It's just your imagination.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:03.620
Besides, our first high school summer vacation is coming up.

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:06.080
Let's all work hard so we can create some good memories, okay?

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:09.620
And if you're ever dumped, I'll introduce you to someone any time.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.290
Be sure to tell us all about your vacation when the new term starts, okay?

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.250
What's up with you two?!

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:28.350
Therefore, I'd like to plan our very first summer Astronomy Club camp.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:32.060
Stars!

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:33.900
I've been waiting for this all along!

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:37.360
Summer equals stars, and stars equals staying up all night!

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:40.530
And staying up all night equals an overnight camping trip!

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:43.910
The Perseids and the Occultation of Pleiades...

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:47.740
It's the perfect time to observe Jupiter's four largest moons too!

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:51.580
This summer's loaded with astrological phenomena!

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:53.170
I'm so looking forward to this!

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:54.920
I know you're happy.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:55.920
Now, calm down.

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:57.130
Camp?

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:58.250
What?!

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:58.250
What?!

00:03:58.550 --> 00:03:59.880
O-O-O-Overnight?

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:01.800
We can do that?

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:03.630
But we're not a sports club.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:05.140
And we don't participate in any tournaments either.

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:08.010
I thought those special privileges were only granted to sports clubs.

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:10.060
That's not true.

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:12.810
We went to a camp last year even though we were the Geology Club.

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:15.150
Even clubs that don't do sports can go on outings.

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:19.230
Although we've got to meet stricter criteria than the sports clubs.

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:22.400
If we go, I'm a little worried about the club budget, but...

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:24.910
But I want to go no matter what!

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:28.580
I want this to become one of our club's traditions, and I hope we can quickly expand!

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:35.790
Eventually, I want ordinary students to also be able to participate in the stargazing night tours we hold.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:30.750
This way please!

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.660
Come this way!

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:36.960
Tours?

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:38.500
Exactly how many people are you planning to take?

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:43.170
Although President Kotodzuka will probably hate us for doing something like that...

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:44.630
Fumin...

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:48.600
Well... she's a nice person.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:52.810
Oh dear. Time's up.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:57.150
Okay, we're off to get permission from the Clubs Council.

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:58.690
Take care of the room, okay?

00:04:59.110 --> 00:04:59.730
Okay!

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:04.860
I wanna go too!

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:05.110
Stop!

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:06.110
You'll ruin our chances!

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:15.330
Hey, hey, Saku-chan, are you positive I don't need to go?

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:18.000
At the very least, they're doing a much better job without you there.

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:20.340
You really think so?

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:30.720
A camp, huh?

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:35.020
I was planning to work hard on ensuring I had plenty of opportunities to spend time with him over the summer,

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:37.190
but this suddenly went beyond that.

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:39.810
But where are these Astronomy Club camps held?

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:41.070
By the ocean? In the mountains?

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:44.490
I've got no idea, but this is definitely a good opportunity.

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:49.280
Even though I joined the Astronomy Club, I've made no progress and summer vacation is already here.

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:52.410
Although there aren't really that many chances to be alone with him right now...

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:54.290
But if we're at the camp...

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:57.250
Hime-chan, watch out!

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:01.960
I'm sorry, Hime-chan!

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:05.090
What do you think you're doing?!

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:08.590
You shouldn't push yourself! Ask for help!

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:09.340
Sorry...

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:11.300
But I just had to do something!

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:13.970
But look! Camping gear!

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:16.810
Tada!

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:18.520
Newspapers, tarp,

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:19.980
bug repellents, mini-games,

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:22.230
star reference book, star chart, flashlights,

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.400
roll-out mat, and finally sleeping bags.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:27.190
Therefore all we need to buy are consumables!

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:28.240
Sleeping bags?

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:30.030
We use sleeping bags?

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:30.530
Yup.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:32.280
I want to stay out all night long.

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:33.830
Sleeping bags are best for that.

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:35.490
Outdoors...

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:38.330
A bag worm... That's not romantic at all...

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:44.340
Now, if we just obtain a telescope and a camera, we'll have all the necessary Astronomy Club gear.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:48.840
We always managed to borrow the Photography Club's equipment thanks to Edogawa.

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:50.760
Although half of the equipment is no good.

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:54.390
I want to take my own photos of the stars while we're at the camp.

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:55.930
Is that possible?

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:57.980
Don't you need professional equipment for that?

00:06:58.730 --> 00:07:01.440
If it's something simple, we can take our own photos.

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:04.860
A lot of amateur photos are featured in astronomy magazines.

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:06.980
See? Aren't these amazing?

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:08.820
Oh?

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:08.820
Oh?

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:12.110
Why am I being sucked into following her lead?

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:14.280
I must not let our age difference get in my way!

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:15.740
Go Hime!

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:18.620
M-More importantly, Ooyagi-kun,

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:21.830
that book you've been reading...

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:23.750
...is that the summer vacation homework assigned by our Modern Japanese class?

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:24.880
Oh, yeah.

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:27.250
Wow, you've started reading it already.

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:29.380
So have you, Makita-san.

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:29.880
Yup.

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:34.850
I never imagined we'd still have to write book reports in high school.

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:37.770
We've got lots of smaller assignments too.

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:39.850
Like this... and that...

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:42.060
It looks hard to do alone.

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:44.690
Oh, they're the same homework assignments as last year!

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:47.940
I still have my work from last year.

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:49.030
Do you want to see them?

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:52.320
No!

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:53.530
That's not the point!

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:55.620
<i>This</i> is what I was waiting for!

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:56.780
Then, shall we do this together?

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:57.620
Are you sure?

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:58.330
<i>Of course.</i>

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:04.710
Hey, why don't we all get together and study from time to time?

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:08.840
And if we all do some stargazing afterwards, we'll be participating in club activities too!

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:10.210
Huh? Wait! Everyone?

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:11.590
Your handout sure brings back memories...

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:14.140
Ko, ki, kuru, kuru, kure, koi...

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:14.140
[Note: This is a Japanese mnemonic to memorize tenses.]

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:13.800
She didn't hear me...

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:18.180
Now that I think about it, we also used to do independent research together, right?

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:20.770
Oh... Like how we used to raise frogs together?

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:21.850
Yup, yup.

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:24.060
Every day was so much fun.

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:27.610
Oh, but we'll be together again this year.

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:29.030
Let's catch them again this year!

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:29.480
Stop it.

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:30.400
I don't want to remember.

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:31.440
Why not?

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:32.740
They're cute!

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:33.610
No, they're not!

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:34.450
Ribbit!

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:37.870
I'm scared of frogs. I'm scared of frogs.

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:39.080
Stop it!

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:40.490
Enough!

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:44.460
Why?

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:46.380
Why do you always get in my way?

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:48.840
You're always close to him...

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:50.960
together like that...

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:52.920
What do you...

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:57.180
What do you, Mihoshi-senpai, think of Ooyagi-kun?

00:08:58.100 --> 00:08:58.350
What?

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:08.730
I-It's nothing...

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:09.900
I love him.

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:16.110
Idiot! W-What are you-

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:19.830
Erm... No.

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:20.790
It's impossible.

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:24.830
Mii-chan, you haven't changed at all since we were little, so...

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:25.290
Yup!

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:28.330
Hime-chan, Saku-chan, Sayochin, and even the President.

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:30.250
I love everyone!

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:38.800
Everyone, sorry for the wait.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:40.550
We've got good news.

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:41.850
Yay!

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:44.100
I went to my monthly photo shoot session.

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:48.900
What's with this awkward atmosphere...

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:50.110
Don't ask me!

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:00.830
Edogawa...

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:04.540
Have you ever been in love with anyone?

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:06.960
Huh? Girls in swimsuits?

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:08.460
Never mind...

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:29.400
Summer Vacation

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:30.400
Ribbit.

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:37.110
This is great!

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:39.320
It's great!

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:40.950
It's perfect!

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:42.410
Now, look this way.

00:10:42.490 --> 00:10:43.950
Seductive yet beautiful...

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:45.870
...and at times, so sharp.

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:49.170
Hey, why are you here too, Edogawa?

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:52.710
Oh, come on. Don't worry about it.

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:55.250
Umm, I peeled some pears.

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:55.920
Would you like some?

00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:57.010
Yes, please!

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:58.340
Be quiet!

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:01.180
Why are you the one who's having the most fun?

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:11.440
We're here!

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:15.650
I wondered where we'd be going since it's a different place from last year.

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:17.190
But it's a nice place.

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:18.570
Is this a lake?

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:20.360
Wow! It looks like the ocean!

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:23.740
It looks like this place is perfect for observations too.

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:31.170
Soon after the first term ended, before we'd even experienced our summer vacation,

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:36.380
the Astronomy Club arrived at a lakeside in northern Japan for our first camp location.

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:39.010
It was timed to coincide with the dark night of the new moon.

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:45.890
Look! Look!

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:46.850
Swan boats!

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:48.560
I love those!

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:53.690
I-It popped into my head...

00:11:54.610 --> 00:11:55.310
I love him.

00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:58.400
It's not something I should be conscious about either...

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:00.900
After all, this is Mii-chan we're talking about.

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:05.780
Summer time in northern Japan is hot, yet cool...

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:07.200
My rhythm is completely off...

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:09.540
Don't worry about it. Don't worry about it.

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:11.460
Now then, let's go!

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:12.620
Let's hurry!

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:15.330
He is concerned after all...

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:18.130
Hey, Astronomy Club!

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:20.010
Muraoka-sensei!

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:22.340
Is everyone here?

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:24.890
I'm sorry I couldn't be with you the whole time.

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:27.720
We're grateful that you even agreed.

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:30.640
Even though I don't do anything, I'm still your vice-advisor, right?

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:34.400
The club I'm an advisor for just happened to have camp at the same time though.

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:39.400
With utmost sarcasm...

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:40.320
Good day.

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:41.190
Fumin!

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:43.450
And the Literature Club members!

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:47.950
I thought that there were noisy kids on the train... to think it was you guys.

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:50.490
I'm glad we were on different carriages.

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:57.080
Our camps may have coincided by coincidence, but make sure you don't cause us trouble.

00:12:57.630 --> 00:12:59.960
You guys are already creating a racket anyway.

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:02.460
What? A racket?!

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:04.340
Yay!

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:06.050
Girls in swimsuits!

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:08.010
Let's hurry up and swim!

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:08.930
Swimsuits!

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:11.520
This place is full of girls in swimsuits!

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:15.390
Shut up!

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:16.900
Hey.

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:18.650
Doesn't he belong to the Photography Club?

00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:20.570
I-I don't know what you're talking about...

00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:23.780
More importantly, our summer house, our summer house...

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:26.070
Let's go to our summer house.

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:28.910
Oh, it's near the lake.

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:31.870
It's a summer house owned by the school.

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:33.410
Souryusou.

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:34.040
Here it is.

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:38.130
It's really beautiful.

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:39.880
Really?

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:41.710
Can we really stay here?

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:43.380
It's spacious too!

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:45.260
It resembles a resort!

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:46.800
Yahoo!

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:48.300
Oh, no, no.

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:49.930
The Astronomy Club gets to stay over there.

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:57.690
It's kind of in ruins...

00:13:58.230 --> 00:13:59.270
Good luck!

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:01.730
I'll be staying in this one.

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:03.230
Sensei!

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:06.860
It's the difference in the number of members and achievements.

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:09.450
But I'll turn a blind eye to the details.

00:14:10.070 --> 00:14:11.530
Well, I wish you luck!

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:15.950
Souryuukan

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:26.840
I won't lose!

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:38.440
It's getting cleaner by the second...

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:46.530
Cleaning complete.

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:47.070
Cleaning

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:47.070
Complete

00:14:55.740 --> 00:14:57.120
Well, good night.

00:14:58.830 --> 00:14:59.750
You're going to sleep?!

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:00.670
What about swimming in the lake?!

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:01.960
The adventure?!

00:15:03.090 --> 00:15:04.840
That's true. It's around the right time.

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:06.510
Let's take a nap.

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:10.680
You know, the nights are what count to the Astronomy Club, right?

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:16.100
Oh, man... I'm so depressed.

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:18.600
I can't sleep yet.

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:20.060
True...

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:25.520
What's that?

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:26.360
Isn't it obvious?

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:29.990
I'm going to peek at the sleeping Sayo-sempai!

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:27.480
Success!

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:31.610
A nap won't do!

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:34.070
In that case, let's go pick up some girls.

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:35.450
Don't worry.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:37.410
It won't be scary if we do it together.

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:41.250
What's more, I hear one's chances are higher at resorts.

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:43.210
Go by yourself!

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:49.380
My rhythm is off...

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:52.130
I love you!

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:54.220
Enough of that already!

00:15:57.810 --> 00:16:00.850
It happens every day anyway, so I shouldn't really worry about it...

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:03.980
Why am I like this?

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:10.820
I can't sleep...

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:21.330
An IT bubble economy for swimsuits!

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:21.330
[Note: This is a parody of the comedian, Hikomaro.]

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:33.800
It's dark...

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:35.800
It's night.

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:43.020
President? Guys?

00:16:56.910 --> 00:16:58.580
The darkness is different...

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:00.990
Is it because the moon's not out?

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:03.540
Because there are so few city lights?

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:08.630
I never knew that nights could be so dark...

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:13.800
Oh, Saku-chan.

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:18.100
Morning. Did you sleep well?

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:22.060
We tried to wake you, but you wouldn't wake up,

00:17:22.140 --> 00:17:23.100
so we let you sleep.

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:26.520
We were just about to call you since supper's ready.

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:29.820
What was that just now?

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:32.320
Saku-kun, don't you think this is amazing?

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:33.820
It was Mihoshi's idea.

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:40.240
She said tonight we wouldn't be watching any bright lights,

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:43.950
but that we'd be watching numerous small lights together.

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:45.750
Amazing, isn't it?

00:17:46.160 --> 00:17:47.790
At first, I was surprised too!

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:49.290
Edogawa...

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:53.210
I'm astonished by your skin too!

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:54.420
I got sunburned.

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:56.220
But don't worry!

00:17:56.470 --> 00:17:57.970
I've prepared everything!

00:17:58.760 --> 00:18:00.260
Let's use the camera and take a picture of the stars!

00:18:00.430 --> 00:18:04.890
Let's forget about the night dew for a moment and take a picture using the tripod-and-release version of the camera!

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:08.560
Isn't this the same camera you were using this morning?

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:11.230
The same camera can be used...

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:13.570
...as long as it comes with either the bulb or timer function.

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:19.240
Now all you need is the switch for the shutter release and a tripod to secure the camera so you can take photographs...

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:20.030
...apparently.

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:22.990
Set the focus to infinity and widen the aperture.

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:25.120
Infinity? Widen?

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:27.290
You'll understand once you try it.

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:29.750
You need both skills and equipment to take a great photograph.

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:31.460
But as long as you can take a photograph, it's a start.

00:18:31.590 --> 00:18:33.050
Well, just watch me!

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:36.210
I had my seniors in the Photography Club teach me.

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:47.930
And then you count 30 seconds exactly...

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:49.600
27... 28...

00:18:49.690 --> 00:18:51.190
29... now!

00:18:55.860 --> 00:18:57.490
You are now captured.

00:18:55.860 --> 00:18:57.530
[Note: A parody of Fist of the Northern Star.]

00:18:57.940 --> 00:19:00.570
Somehow... they seem to have taught you something unnecessary...

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:17.050
Let's start soon.

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:20.050
To the lakeside we go!

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:41.200
The Astronomy Club's very first summer camp: First Night.

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:43.410
The Milky Way!

00:20:11.350 --> 00:20:12.100
What is this?

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:13.810
They're twinkling.

00:20:15.690 --> 00:20:16.860
Amazing.

00:20:19.320 --> 00:20:20.900
It's like a planetarium.

00:20:23.610 --> 00:20:26.830
We've been outside using candle light only, so our eyes have already adapted.

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:33.040
In the dark night, I somehow recognized Mii-chan's smile.

00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:43.720
Ooyagi-kun...

00:20:44.550 --> 00:20:45.140
Um...

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:48.180
I'm sorry for saying something strange the other day.

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:51.180
Our long awaited summer camp has finally begun...

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:55.400
...so I'm concerned that you're still worrying over that...

00:20:55.770 --> 00:20:57.020
I'm sorry too.

00:20:57.360 --> 00:20:58.980
Somehow, I managed to worry you.

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:05.320
More like... I don't actually know what you said due to my fear of frogs.

00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:06.490
What?!

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:10.790
This doesn't happen often, so let's enjoy ourselves.

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:15.750
When I watch her, I kind of feel a little foolish.

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:18.670
She's always saying, "I'll show you something special tonight too."

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:20.090
That "it'll be fun."

00:21:20.590 --> 00:21:22.840
With the exact same expression she had that summer vacation back when we were kids.

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:26.300
Although outwardly, I pretended to hate it;

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:29.010
deep inside, I was excited to see what was there.

00:21:29.810 --> 00:21:32.140
It was like I was some accomplice running through the night.

00:21:33.640 --> 00:21:35.940
When I think of that, I somehow...

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:40.110
Well, I don't really know how to explain it...

00:21:43.320 --> 00:21:43.990
It's okay.

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:46.360
Then, are we all accomplices tonight?

00:21:46.570 --> 00:21:47.490
Yay!

00:21:47.740 --> 00:21:48.200
Yup.

00:21:50.700 --> 00:21:54.870
An accomplice who shares the jewel in the night sky, hidden by the dark.

00:21:55.080 --> 00:22:01.340
The Starry Sky we saw that day excited me,

00:22:01.800 --> 00:22:06.300
since when have I forgotten it?

00:22:04.130 --> 00:22:05.220
Kotodzuka-senpai?

00:22:06.380 --> 00:22:08.220
What are you worried about?

00:22:08.340 --> 00:22:09.390
What are you talking about?

00:22:08.430 --> 00:22:14.270
The wind and my faint memories washed by the waves of time

00:22:09.760 --> 00:22:10.680
It's time to switch the lights off.

00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:19.100
rusted my tears and words…

00:22:19.150 --> 00:22:22.440
We stayed outside until morning.

00:22:22.520 --> 00:22:26.610
I’ve hid my heart within

00:22:26.570 --> 00:22:30.030
From time to time, whenever we got frightened from the vast depth of the sky, we screamed out loud.

00:22:28.360 --> 00:22:33.240
a hope with no destination out of fear…

00:22:30.660 --> 00:22:31.660
Ina Bauer!

00:22:30.660 --> 00:22:31.660
[Note: A skating technique that became famous in Japan after Arakawa Shizuka won gold at the 2006 winter Olympics.]

00:22:34.370 --> 00:22:41.630
The wish I entrusted to the sky

00:22:36.040 --> 00:22:37.910
Look, it's a satellite.

00:22:38.540 --> 00:22:40.380
That means it'll be morning soon.

00:22:41.630 --> 00:22:49.260
is released through the heavens!

00:22:50.430 --> 00:22:57.180
This endlessly overflowing emotion

00:22:57.730 --> 00:23:03.820
illuminates my feelings for you and disappears.

00:23:04.520 --> 00:23:11.360
But like a Star blooming in darkness,

00:23:11.360 --> 00:23:15.620
it will one day shine brightly!

00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:22.580
Probably... The next time we hear the word "morning," we'll be thinking of this morning.

00:23:23.080 --> 00:23:24.290
Thinking that...

00:23:35.810 --> 00:23:36.180
W-

00:23:38.140 --> 00:23:38.770
W-What...

00:23:40.100 --> 00:23:42.480
What are you guys doing?!

00:23:52.530 --> 00:23:56.870
I look up at the sky, and I think of you…

00:23:57.160 --> 00:24:00.540
but I can’t find the words,

00:24:01.710 --> 00:24:03.880
I want to tell you,

00:24:03.880 --> 00:24:06.380
but they just slip away…

00:24:06.670 --> 00:24:10.050
almost like Shooting Stars.

00:24:10.550 --> 00:24:14.640
In this Wave of Silence,

00:24:15.010 --> 00:24:19.020
a ray of light flickers the darkness

00:24:19.470 --> 00:24:24.310
playing with my memories

00:24:24.310 --> 00:24:30.150
and releasing my heart.

00:24:30.990 --> 00:24:33.070
Into the future,

00:24:33.070 --> 00:24:41.660
I will have these feelings again!

00:24:42.080 --> 00:24:46.080
No worries, I’m not alone.

00:24:46.330 --> 00:24:51.170
You have taught me I’m not alone.

00:24:51.170 --> 00:25:00.060
Listen to my “Twinkle” story!

00:25:00.220 --> 00:25:04.230
Maybe my voice would reach you.

00:25:05.600 --> 00:25:10.480
I look up at the sky, surrounded by Stardust!

00:25:15.030 --> 00:25:20.040
Next time: The Star of Words

00:25:15.950 --> 00:25:18.830
Next time, on Sora no Manimani: The Star of Words.

00:25:19.410 --> 00:25:20.200
What?!

00:25:20.040 --> 00:25:25.040
"Illicit sexual relationships" (lol) detected

00:25:20.040 --> 00:25:25.040
in the Astronomy Club.

00:25:25.040 --> 00:25:30.040
Being banned from nightly activities,

00:25:25.040 --> 00:25:30.040
what will the Astronomy Club do?!
